17. Observability
            
            The gateway sees virtually every request.
            
            Therefore it's a natural place to collect:            
                              request count
                              latency
                              status code
                              client
                              API
                              region
                              rate-limit violations
                              authentication failures
            
            For example:            
                  GET /orders
                  200 → 120 ms
                  
                  POST /payment
                  500 → 800 ms
            
                  GET /users
                  429 → rate limited
            
            This gives us a global picture.            
                  Google's API Gateway architecture includes logging, monitoring, and tracing around gateway requests.


===============================================================================================================================================
18. Request tracing
      This is particularly important in microservices.
      
      Suppose:      
                  Client
                    |
                    v
                  Gateway
                    |
                    v
                  Order Service
                    |
                    v
                  Payment Service
                    |
                    v
                  Inventory Service
      
      The request should carry a correlation/trace ID: traceId = abc123
      
      Then we can see:      
                        abc123
                        
                        Gateway       5ms
                        Order        30ms
                        Payment     100ms
                        Inventory    20ms
                        
                        Total       155ms
      
      Without distributed tracing, debugging becomes painful.
============================================================================================================================================
19. Retry — be careful here

            A gateway can retry some failed requests.
            But this is a dangerous area.

            Suppose: POST /payment
                        Gateway sends request.

            Payment service processes it successfully.

            But response gets lost.

            Gateway sees: timeout

            If gateway blindly retries: POST /payment   the payment could happen twice.

            So:
                  Retries should depend on idempotency and operation semantics.

            For example: GET /products   is usually safe to retry.

            But:  POST /payment  may require an idempotency key.

            This is a very strong L5 point.


===============================================================================================================================================
20. Timeouts

            Never allow:            
                              Gateway
                                 |
                                 v
                              Backend
                                 |
                                 | hangs for 5 minutes
                                 |
            to consume gateway resources indefinitely.

            Set deadlines: Gateway timeout = 2 sec
            
            If backend hasn't responded: 504 Gateway Timeout
      
      But the timeout needs to be designed based on the API's SLA.
      
      Don't blindly make every API 2 seconds.
===============================================================================================================================================
21. Circuit Breaker
            
            Suppose Payment Service is unhealthy.
            
            Without protection:                              
                              Gateway
                                 |
                                 +--> Payment ❌
                                 +--> Payment ❌
                                 +--> Payment ❌
                                 +--> Payment ❌
                                 +--> Payment ❌
            
            We keep sending requests to a failing service.
            
            Circuit breaker can transition:
            
                                          CLOSED
                                             ↓
                                          Failures increase
                                             ↓
                                          OPEN
                                             ↓
                                          Stop sending traffic
                                             ↓
                                          After cooldown
                                             ↓
                                          HALF OPEN
                                             ↓
                                          Test request
                                             ↓
                                          Healthy → CLOSED
            
            This protects the failing service and prevents cascading failures.



